Subject: [PATCH 01942/11362] [conductor] PHASE A1 (HEADLINE; the DATA-SPARSITY
 fix) -- GROW the labeled ARC candidate pool so the oracle-distinct aggregator
 has minority-correct evidence to learn from. .392's ARC tie was diagnosed
 DATA-SPARSITY: only 20 positive/correct candidates across 28419 (base-rate
 0.0007), wrong_majority_n 0-9 on the held-out split -- too few
 minority-correct examples to learn or test a wrong-majority recoverer. FIX:
 assemble the MAXIMAL cached pool (ALL GAP-4 stage2 games + the GAP-4 induced
 programs + the existing 28419 candidate set), dedupe + relabel is_correct
 (candidate grid == gold/induced pred_grid), GROUPED by task_id; and IF
 positives remain below target, a BOUNDED candidate TOP-UP via the cached
 explore-induce-verify solver (exp4236) on the wrong-majority tasks (cap
 candidates/task + tasks to FIT THE WINDOW; honest partial if the cap is
 reached). Target: >=40 wrong-majority held-out tasks (oracle@K>vote@1) and a
 meaningfully larger positive_candidate_n than .392's 20. Report
 arc_pool_grown (BARE bool) + positive_candidate_n + wrong_majority_n +
 held_out_task_n + pool_artifact_path. NO TRM training; READ-ONLY w.r.t. the
 TRM checkpoint.

